# Web UI and state

This Cursor rule supplements the repository AGENTS.md instructions. It may add scoped requirements but may not weaken root security invariants.

**Authority:** [`apps/web/AGENTS.md`](../../apps/web/AGENTS.md) · root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md)

## Do not

- Handle secrets or keys on the main thread
- Sign or broadcast without `openSignConfirmDialog`
- Shortcut the send flow (build → preview → confirm → worker sign → optional broadcast)
- Introduce a new UI or state-management library
- Hand-roll controls when `components/ui` already provides them
- Copy to clipboard without `copyWithClear`

Worker entry under `apps/web/src/workers/` also follows [`core-and-worker.mdc`](core-and-worker.mdc).

## Structure

- Pages: `routes/` · features: `features/` · primitives: `components/ui/`
- Zustand: session/settings/network/ui · React Query: RPC/prices

## Pattern anchors

### BAD

```tsx
const signed = await worker.signTransaction(tx);
await broadcast(signed); // no user confirmation
```

### GOOD

```tsx
const confirmed = await openSignConfirmDialog({ summary });
if (!confirmed) return;
const signed = await worker.signTransaction(tx);
await broadcast(signed);
```
